# Ship Windows .exe for Plex PC users

After meaningful hub features that users need on the Plex PC (new UI panels, desktop packaging, settings that only matter in the installed app):

1. Bump `version` in `package.json` when shipping a new release.
2. Build the installer: `npm run dist:win` (set `NODE_OPTIONS=--use-system-ca` if Electron/npm downloads fail TLS on this machine).
3. Create/tag a GitHub Release `vX.Y.Z` and upload the NSIS installer from `release/` (`Arrs Hub-x.y.z-x64.exe`). Include the portable build if present. Release notes should note that no Node/Git is required to run the app.
4. Copy the NSIS installer to `G:\My Drive\exe\` (create the folder if needed). Keep the version in the filename. Overwrite older copies of the same version if re-shipping.
5. **Never commit** `release/`, `.exe` files, or other large binaries to git.
6. Commit the version bump (and rule/README updates if any), then push `main`.

Do this at natural stop points when the Plex PC needs the new build — not after every tiny edit. Source still goes to GitHub; the Drive `exe\` folder is the easy grab for home installs alongside Releases.
